kend pool.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-0022-metrics-backend-pool\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"Query backend pool_waiters over 2026-10-01T11:45:00Z-2026-10-01T13:00:00Z to check whether backend pool pressure rises co-timed with any payment-side inflation.\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"backend\", \"metric_names\": [\"pool_waiters\"], \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:45:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\"}, \"reason\": \"payment_external_timeout predicts that backend pool_waiters grow because backend threads block on payment calls, so the co-timed pool_waiters series is the direct discriminator between payment-driven pool pressure and the observed backend db_pool_max reduction.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Rising backend pool_waiters synchronized with payment inflation supports the payment-driven explanation; pool_waiters behaviour independent of payment keeps the cause local to the backend pool.\"}], \"optional_checks\": [], \"cited_evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1001-E-001\", \"incident_1001-E-003\", \"incident_1001-E-004\", \"incident_1001-E-005\", \"incident_1001-E-007\", \"incident_1001-E-008\", \"incident_1001-T-backend\", \"incident_1001-T-payment\"], \"rationale\": \"The latest decision is INVESTIGATE (round 3), which selects no hypothesis for FINALIZE, so the best grounded existing candidate is reviewed: backend_pool_config_regression (hyp-2354bf4d3f473cedacf9117199ff63a5928dab8fb231824dd4f90ea588ae234e), the only candidate marked SUPPORTED and backed by two or more independent sources (metrics, changes, configs, logs, topology). Its cause discriminator is observed: incident_1001-E-003 records the runtime-1 'Runtime settings deployment applied' change at 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z and incident_1001-E-004 shows db_pool_max reduced from 20 to 2 with concurrency=120, and the matching backend symptoms follow it (pool_waiters=118 at incident_1001-E-005 and a deadline-exceeded log at incident_1001-E-008) against a 